{"id":56406,"ord":148,"n_segments":182,"prev":56405,"next":56407,"doc":{"id":"68113","title":"68113_Barney Bigard oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Albany Leon \"Barney\" Bigard","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68113/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68113"},"chapter":"Recording sessions 1926-33","title":"Films in the discography: 'Bundle of Blues' and 'Belle of the Nineties'","category":"recording_session","summary":"Willard asks about early films; he does not recall 'Bundle of Blues' and identifies 'Belle of the Nineties' as Mae West's film.","period":"1933-34","year_from":1933,"year_to":1933,"words":120,"start":[169,8],"end":[170,7],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68113#s56406","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Mae West","qid":"Q202878","n":3},{"name":"Duke Ellington","qid":"Q4030","n":1}],"story":{"theme":29,"theme_name":"Jazz musicians in the movies and film scoring","community":55,"community_name":"Jazz musicians on film and studio scoring","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":169,"b":8,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Looking at this discography I see a reference to a film \"Bundle of Blues.\""},{"p":169,"b":9,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"\"Bundle of Blues?\""},{"p":169,"b":10,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Uh-huh. What was that?"},{"p":169,"b":11,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"I don't know."},{"p":169,"b":12,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"It says 1933."},{"p":169,"b":13,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Oh, that's when I was a youngster."},{"p":169,"b":14,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"(Laughter) I know that."},{"p":169,"b":15,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"\"Bundle of Blues?\""},{"p":169,"b":16,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Bande du the film \"Bundle of Blues.\""},{"p":169,"b":17,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"All right, well.\nThen the next films mentioned are \"Belle of the Nineties\" and \"Symphony in Black.\""},{"p":169,"b":18,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"You remember \"Belle of the Nineties\", don't you?"},{"p":169,"b":19,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"With who?"},{"p":169,"b":20,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Oh, I think that was when you were with"},{"p":170,"b":0,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Duke. April 1934."},{"p":170,"b":1,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"That must be Mae West, I think."},{"p":170,"b":2,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"I think so."},{"p":170,"b":3,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah."},{"p":170,"b":4,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"That was a Mae West film, wasn't it?"},{"p":170,"b":5,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah, Mae West. Yeah, sure."},{"p":170,"b":6,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"She was quite a character."},{"p":170,"b":7,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"She was a --"}]}